{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Upon the two shoulder-pieces below.</b> The settings are placed at the heads of the upper shoulder-pieces of the ephod that come upon his shoulders, opposite his neck, and they fold down and hang to his front. And He commanded to put the [other] two rings at their head — that is, the one joined to the ephod. And that which is said ״לְעֻמַּת מַחְבַּרְתּוֹ״ — adjacent to the place of their joining on the ephod, slightly above the band; for the joining is opposite the band, but these are placed slightly up the rise of the shoulder-pieces. That is what is meant by ״מִמַּעַל לְחֵשֶׁב הָאֵפוֹד.״ And they are opposite the bottom edge of the breastplate. And he puts a cord of tekhelet through those rings and through the rings of the breastplate and laces them together with that cord, right and left, so that the lower edge of the breastplate does not slip forward and swing back and knock against his belly — and so it sits properly upon the robe." "<b>Opposite its face.</b> On the outer side."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The feminine plural suffix in נְתוּנוֹת refers to the settings (מִשְׁבְּצוֹת); the feminine plural in הַבָּאִים/בָּאִים and their modifiers throughout refers to the shoulder-pieces (כִתְפוֹת), consistent with Rashi's usage."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:19.858223055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}